I want to be able to have a flat acceleration profile on mice and adaptive acceleration on trackpads.

The config might look something like this:
```conf
input {
    accel_profile=flat
    touchpad {
        accel_profile=adaptive
        natural_scroll=yes
        tap-to-click=yes
    }
}
````

Here was my previous nix home configuration.
```nix
{
  wayland.windowManager.hyprland = {
    enable = true;
    systemdIntegration = true;
    extraConfig = builtins.readFile ./hyprland.conf;
  };
}
```

Occasionally, I found commands triggered by `hyprland-session.target` such as `waybar` doesn't have the desired ` WAYLAND_DISPLAY`, `HYPRLAND_INSTANCE_SIGNATURE`, etc., environment variables. It seemed to be caused by the two detached commands below raced, and the later command was executed before the side effects of the first command.

https://github.com/hyprwm/Hyprland/blob/a69fd21a1ac90c24cee659595d62329f8638d632/nix/hm-module.nix#L105-L106

I fixed this by using the following home configuration.

```nix
{
  wayland.windowManager.hyprland = {
    enable = true;
    systemdIntegration = false;
    extraConfig = ''
      exec-once = export WAYLAND_DISPLAY DISPLAY && ${pkgs.dbus}/bin/dbus-update-activation-environment --systemd DISPLAY WAYLAND_DISPLAY HYPRLAND_INSTANCE_SIGNATURE XDG_CURRENT_DESKTOP && systemctl --user start hyprland-session.target
    '' + builtins.readFile ./hyprland.conf;
  };
  # following lines are copied from nix/hw-module.nix
  systemd.user.targets.hyprland-session = ...;
}
```

