### Description

Commit c36c30c breaks my config. I'm running on the `nixos-23.05` channel where this option does not exist yet, resulting in an error. This could probably be fixed using version checks and `lib.mkIf`.

### How to reproduce

Try building a nixosConfiguration with the latest Hyprland NixOS module, using `nixos-23.05` as the `nixpkgs` channel or flake input. Example with flakes:

```nix
{
  inputs = {
    nixpkgs.url = "github:nixos/nixpkgs/nixos-23.05";
    hyprland.url = "github:hyprwm/Hyprland";
  };

  outputs = { nixpkgs, hyprland, ... }: {
    nixosConfigurations.default = nixpkgs.lib.nixosSystem {
      system = "x86_64-linux";
      modules = [
        # All of this is needed for `nix flake check` to pass in any case
        {
          fileSystems."/" = {
            device = "/dev/disk/by-label/nixos";
            fsType = "ext4";
          };

          boot.loader.grub.devices = [ "nodev" ];

          system.stateVersion = "23.05";
        }


        hyprland.nixosModules.default
        { programs.hyprland.enable = true; }
      ];
    };
  };
}
```
And run `nix flake check`.

